The platform files here (the Python in components/, the YAML files and the scripts) and the shim sources under
components/*/shim are written by Fox Red Labs and licensed under the BSD-3-Clause license of the repository's
root LICENSE. The shim sources do not stand alone: they replace the hardware layer of ESPHome and are
compiled together with ESPHome's C++ runtime (esphome/core and the components), which is licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 (ESPHome's Python code is MIT). A firmware image built from this folder
is therefore a combined work under GPLv3, and anyone who passes that image on must offer its complete
corresponding source under GPLv3, which includes these shim sources and any change made to ESPHome. The
image also links Texas Instruments SDK code and libraries under their own licenses; check each for
compatibility with GPLv3 before passing an image on. Reading, copying or reusing the source files in this folder on their own is covered by the BSD-3-Clause
license only.
